          }
        },
        "text_VnAwbf": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-md",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-0",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-0",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<h4><strong>Why Nontoxic Air Care Products Matter<\/strong><\/h4><p><\/p><p><strong>Nontoxic air care products<\/strong> are made from safe, plant-based ingredients and avoid harsh chemicals that can negatively affect pets. They’re designed to neutralize odors rather than mask them.<\/p><p>Benefits include:<\/p><ol><li>Safe for use around pets, kids, and sensitive individuals<\/li><li>Made without synthetic chemicals<\/li><li>Often biodegradable and packaged sustainably<\/li><li>Free from allergens and hormone-disrupting additives<\/li><\/ol><p> <\/p><h4><strong>Creating Air That’s Optimized for Pet Health<\/strong><\/h4><p><\/p><p>Beyond odor elimination, think about the <strong>overall air quality<\/strong> in your home. Pet dander, dust, and allergens can stay airborne for hours, contributing to sneezing, asthma, and general discomfort.<\/p><p>Here’s how to improve your air for both you and your furry family members:<\/p><p><strong>1. Invest in a High-Quality Air Purifier<\/strong><\/p><p>An<strong> air purifier<\/strong> is one of the most effective tools for improving air quality. It captures:<\/p><ol><li>Pet dander<\/li><li>Odors<\/li><li>Hair and fur<\/li><li>Dust <\/li><li>Pollen<\/li><li>Smoke<\/li><li>Mold spores allergen<\/li><li>Bacteria<\/li><li>Viruses<\/li><\/ol><p><\/p><p>Some models even include <strong>activated carbon filters<\/strong>, which are excellent for neutralizing pet odors specifically. Choose a purifier rated for the size of your space and run it continuously in high-traffic pet areas.<\/p><p><strong>2. Use Environmentally Friendly Air Care Products<\/strong><\/p><p>Eco-friendly doesn’t have to mean less effective. Many<strong> air care products<\/strong> are now designed with pets in mind, using natural ingredients and refillable or recyclable packaging.<\/p><p>Great options include:<\/p><ol><li>Refillable essential oil diffusers<\/li><li>Soy or beeswax candles with pet-safe scents<\/li><li>Baking soda-based deodorizing sprays<\/li><li>Charcoal odor absorbers<\/li><\/ol><p><\/p><p><strong>3. Ventilate and Clean Regularly<\/strong><\/p><p>While air care products help, fresh air is still key. Open windows, run fans, and clean pet bedding often. Combine this with air purifying solutions to maintain truly clean, breathable air.<\/p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
